{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copies selected take names, one per line, in REAPER selection order. Requires SWS/S&M. Items without an active take are skipped.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copies selected track names, one per line, in REAPER selection order. Requires SWS/S&M.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Applies one clipboard line to each selected take, in REAPER selection order. Requires SWS/S&M. Empty lines clear names; a final newline is ignored. Items without an active take are skipped, matching the copy action.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Applies one clipboard line to each selected track, in REAPER selection order. Requires SWS/S&M. Empty lines clear names; a final newline is ignored. Extra lines are ignored; unmatched tracks keep their names.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates one track below the source track for each selected item with an active take. Uses take names and selection order. Skips locked items and items without a take. New tracks remain inside the source track folder; folder-parent items move to new children.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Reposition Item Groups with Curved Gap\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Groups selected items into batches of N and repositions each batch with a fixed or curved (accelerating/decelerating) gap between batches. Selected items sharing a REAPER group ID form one logical unit and shift together across tracks. Unselected group members are not moved. The script remembers your last-used settings.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Set Start Gap = End Gap for a uniform gap between all batches.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Set Items per group = 1 to apply a gap between every individual item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Spacing Mode 'end': gap is measured from the end of the last item in the previous batch (default). 'start': from the start of its first item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Curve > 1 delays the change from Start Gap to End Gap; Curve < 1 advances it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Negative gaps are allowed. Locked selections abort without moving anything.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Selected tracks supply reference spans from all their items. Selecting a folder includes its own items and every nested descendant track. Overlapping and touching reference spans are merged across all reference tracks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Selected items are the targets. They are split at reference boundaries, and portions outside the reference spans are deleted, including targets entirely outside those spans. Reference items cover themselves and remain unchanged. Surviving target pieces remain selected; other selections are preserved.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Empty reference sets abort safely. Locked targets are skipped and counted. Native item splitting preserves take sources, offsets, and playback rates. Changes share one undo entry. If splitting fails, no gaps are deleted; use Undo to restore any partial splits before correcting the error and retrying.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Adds markers at each selected item end, plus an offset in project seconds. Choose t for active-take markers or p for project markers. Empty names are allowed. Take positions include the source offset and playback rate. Takes with stretch markers are skipped; use project markers for warped audio.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Adds markers at each selected item start, plus an offset in project seconds. Choose t for active-take markers or p for project markers. Empty names are allowed. Take positions include the source offset and playback rate. Takes with stretch markers are skipped; use project markers for warped audio.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates one named, colored region spanning all items directly on each selected track. Empty tracks are skipped. Folder children are not included by this action.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copies a four-key [HitObjects] section to the clipboard. Requires SWS/S&M. Track names 1-4 select columns. Active take names must be type,hitsound. Supported types: 1 or 5 (tap), 128 (hold). Hitsounds: 0-15. The earliest selected item anchors time zero, including invalid items. This exports hit objects, not a complete .osu beatmap.\par}
}
